  "problem": {
    "id": "train-6935",
    "question": "An air conditioner running for eight hours would consume 7.2 kilowatts. How many kilowatts would the air conditioner consume if it was used for 6 hours a day for 5 days?",
    "gold": "27",
    "answer": "The air conditioner consumes 7.2/8 = <<7.2/8=0.9>>0.9 kilowatt per hour.\nSo, in 6 hours, it will consume 0.9 kilowatts per hour * 6 hours = <<0.9*6=5.4>>5.4 kilowatts.\nIn 5 days, its total consumption is 5.4 kilowatts * 5 = <<5.4*5=27>>27 kilowatts.\n#### 27"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many kilowatts the air conditioner would consume if it was used for 6 hours a day for 5 days, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the daily consumption:**\n   - The air conditioner consumes 7.2 kilowatts in 8 hours.\n   - To find the daily consumption, we need to determine how much it consumes in 6 hours.\n   - We can set up a proportion to find the daily consumption:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{7.2 \\text{ kilowatts}}{8 \\text{ hours}} = \\frac{x \\text{ kilowatts}}{6 \\text{ hours}}\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\( x \\):\n     \\[\n     x = \\frac{7.2 \\text{ kilowatts} \\times 6 \\text{ hours}}{8 \\text{ hours}} = \\frac{43.2 \\text{ kilowatt-hours}}{8} = 5.4 \\text{ kilowatts}\n     \\]\n   - So, the air conditioner consumes 5.4 kilowatts per day.\n\n2. **Calculate the total consumption for 5 days:**\n   - Now that we know the air conditioner consumes 5.4 kilowatts per day, we can find the total consumption for 5 days:\n     \\[\n     5.4 \\text{ kilowatts/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 27 \\text{ kilowatt-hours}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the air conditioner would consume \\(\\boxed{27}\\) kilowatts if it was used for 6 hours a day for 5 days.",
